  "notes": "Fitted 2026-11-16 by fit_race_interaction.py from end-of-lap on-road gaps (one sample per lap). dirty_air.time_loss_s is seconds per lap for a car whose gap to the car ahead at the end of lap is below window_s, vs clean air, from two-way fixed effects (stint, race-lap). overtake probability is per lap for a car directly behind within overtake.window_s: p = sigmoid(intercept + pace_delta_coef*pace_delta + tyre_age_delta_coef*tyre_age_delta + gap_coef*gap + track_offset[track]); pace_delta = defender pace - attacker pace in s/lap (positive = attacker faster, tyre/fuel-normalised car pace), tyre_age_delta = defender age - attacker age (positive = attacker fresher). Use track_offset = 0 for tracks not listed. pass_time_cost_s is the extra lap time on the lap the pass is recorded, beyond the dirty-air term, relative to clean air (may be negative). lap1 mean/sd are (end-of-lap-1 position - grid position); positive = lost places. min_follow_gap_s is the 5th percentile of sustained-follower gaps at timing-line resolution."
